    "media:imagetext": "American Federation of Labor and Congress of Industrial Organizations\nEXECUTIVE COUNCIL\no1b sixteenth Sifeet. Nw\nLANE KIRKLAND PRESIDENT\nTHOMAS R. DONAHUE SECRETARY TRFASURER\nwasnington. D.C. 2000d\n1202) 637.5000\nApril 11, 1986\nMs. Edith Lauterbach\n%Association of Flight Attendants\n162) Massachusetts Avenue, N.W.\nWashington, D.C. 20036\nDear Sister Lauterbach:\nThe word is out that you are hanging up your wings and putting away your rolling\nsuitcase. After 42 years of helping curious, nervous and sometimes obnoxious passengers\nto feel comfortable in the sky, you are going to enjoy life in the beautiful city on the bay.\nAll of your friends in the labor movement join me in wishing you many pleasant\nyears of full-time relaxation and pursuit of purely personal pleasures; you deserve them.\ncareer, you were never content simply to watch the world whiz\nby the cabin windows.\nDuring your lon ou helped make changes, changes for the better for co-workers\nand many others by your leadership in building the organization that is now the\nAssociation of Flight Attendants.\nYou proved that a trade union is an instrument for\nbringing dignity, fairness and gender equality to the work place.\nWe were especially proud and pleased that you took part in the ceremony when\nthe American Federation of Labor and Congress of Industrial Organizations issued its\ncharter of affiliation to the AFA, a milestone in the honored history of the labor\nmovement.\nGood luck and best wishes!\nSincerely and fraternally,\nSame Pille O\nPresident",
